{
 "_comment": [
  "Model registry. One row per model that can appear in the serving mix, plus reference rows.",
  "weights: 'open' = downloadable weights (a published HF repo); 'closed' = API only.",
  "tier: 'frontier' = a lab model that can sit in a frontier basket (assumptions.json names the baskets);",
  "'other-closed' = closed model shown for reference only; 'excluded' = stealth/unknown; open rows have no tier.",
  "aliases: every OpenRouter spelling (slug; dated permaslugs and :free/:batch variants are stripped by the collector).",
  "inferencex: the display-model name InferenceX's public API accepts for THIS model (its own runs). Only rows with an",
  "inferencex name can carry serving tokens: no family curves and no parameter proxies stand in for a missing benchmark.",
  "A row whose name has runs only under another workload (e.g. agentic traces) is excluded under the 8k/1k workload.",
  "Parameter counts (total_b, active_b) come from each lab's Hugging Face model card (url); they are shown, not used",
  "in the arithmetic. read_on is when the row was last checked.",
  "inferencex_family: for the 'estimated' throughput scope only, the benchmark-only registry row whose InferenceX curve stands in",
  "for this model (same architecture). Rows with tier 'benchmark-only' are not routable; they exist for the parameter fit and",
  "as family curves. trace_family: which model family in data/traces.json supplies this model's per-task token volumes",
  "(anthropic = claude-opus-4-5, openai = gpt-5.2, deepseek = DeepSeek-V3.2, kimi = Kimi-K2.5, open_avg = run-weighted mean of",
  "the open-weight families)."
 ],
